+# --- Email -------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Two ways to send; SMTP wins over Resend when both are set.
+#
+# SMTP_USER is always a FULL login, never a bare local part — a bare "info"
+# authenticates against nothing and the server refuses to relay, which presents
+# as "receiving works but sending does not".
+#
+# BREVO is what this deploy uses: smtp-relay.brevo.com, port 587.
+#   SMTP_USER is Brevo's own generated login (…@smtp-brevo.com) and NOT the
+#   address in MAIL_FROM. MAIL_FROM may be any address on a domain
+#   authenticated under Brevo -> Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs; the mailbox
+#   behind it does not need to exist for sending to work.
+#   The catch is the other direction: nothing receives mail at that address, so
+#   a member hitting reply gets a bounce. Until a real mailbox exists, keep
+#   a working address in the message body.
+#
+# A HOSTINGER MAILBOX is the alternative: smtp.hostinger.com, 465 (SSL) or
+#   587 (STARTTLS), SMTP_USER being the address itself. Replies reach a person,
+#   which is the reason to prefer it. The trade is volume — mailbox plans cap
+#   daily sends, so a month-end invoice run to every member can hit the cap and
+#   the rest fail quietly. Watch the logs the first time a full run goes out.
+SMTP_HOST=
+SMTP_PORT=587
+SMTP_USER=
+SMTP_PASS=
+SMTP_SECURE=
+MAIL_FROM="Fit Generations Gym <info@fitgenerationsgym.com>"
+
+# Resend — HTTP API, no mailbox. Used only when SMTP is unset.
+RESEND_API_KEY=
+
 # --- PayHero (recommended) ---------------------------------------------------
 # STK push that settles straight into the gym's bank account. The member still
 # approves an M-Pesa prompt — "bank" is where the money lands, not how they pay.
